  K1: (i) True, (ii) True, (iii) D True, (iii) D' True, flat d_t True -> PASS

K2 matter kinetic structure. About a background with A_rel = y0 (u = |y0|/a0) and baryons at rest, a uniform
   displacement xi(t) changes A_rel by xi'' (K1(d); D' likewise through a_b). P has no time derivative in (A),
   so at gamma_L = 0 P is eliminated: L_matter = rho xi'^2/2 + J(|y0 + c xi''|) - k xi^2/2 (c = 1; M2: c = 0).
  Hessian of J in xi'' : along A_rel -1/(K*(u + 1)**2) ; across A_rel -1/(K*(u + 1)) ; off-diagonal 0
  linearized Euler-Lagrange: -k*xi(t) - rho*Derivative(xi(t), (t, 2)) - Derivative(xi(t), (t, 4))/K = 0
  characteristic polynomial in s (xi ~ e^(s t)): -(K*k + K*rho*s**2 + s**4)/K;  s^2 roots: [-sqrt(K)*sqrt(K*rho**2 - 4*k)/2 - K*rho/2, sqrt(K)*sqrt(K*rho**2 - 4*k)/2 - K*rho/2]
  Ostrogradsky Hamiltonian (q1 = xi, q2 = xi', p2 = H xi''): H_O = -K*p2**2/2 + k*q1**2/2 + p1*q2 - q2**2*rho/2;  d^2 H_O/dp1^2 = 0  -> linear in p1, unbounded below when the H xi''^2 term is present (H != 0)

